     With[0m[2m this approach[0m[2m:
     -[0m[2m First[0m[2m call:[0m[2m `[0m[2mdecrement[0m[2m_order`[0m[2m (de[0m[2mcre[0m[2mments,[0m[2m marks[0m[2m processed),[0m[2m `charge[0m[2m` ([0m[2mnew,[0m[2m succeeds),[0m[2m SUCCESS[0m[2m
     - Duplicate[0m[2m call:[0m[2m `de[0m[2mcrement_order[0m[2m` ([0m[2malready processed[0m[2m, returns[0m[2m True),[0m[2m `charge[0m[2m` ([0m[2malready charged[0m[2m, returns[0m[2m True),[0m[2m SUCCESS[0m[2m
     
     No[0m[2m double delivery[0m[2m! The[0m[2m duplicate[0m[2m call[0m[2m returns True[0m[2m without changing[0m[2m anything.[0m[2m This is[0m[2m id[0m[2mempotent and[0m[2m correct.[0m[2m
     
     And[0m[2m for[0m[2m the retry[0m[2m-after[0m[2m-cr[0m[2mash[0m[2m scenario:[0m[2m
     -[0m[2m First call[0m[2m:[0m[2m `de[0m[2mcrement_order[0m[2m` ([0m[2mdecre[0m[2mments,[0m[2m marks processed[0m[2m), CR[0m[2mASH before[0m[2m charge[0m[2m
     -[0m[2m Retry[0m[2m: `[0m[2mdecrement[0m[2m_order`[0m[2m (already[0m[2m processed,[0m[2m returns True[0m[2m), `[0m[2mcharge`[0m[2m (new[0m[2m, might[0m[2m succeed or[0m[2m fail)[0m[2m
     
     If charge[0m[2m succeeds:[0m[2m SUCCESS,[0m[2m item[0m[2m delivered,[0m[2m customer[0m[2m charged.[0m[2m Correct[0m[2m!
     If[0m[2m charge fails[0m[2m: returns[0m[2m False,[0m[2m but inventory[0m[2m is[0m[2m already decre[0m[2mmented.[0m[2m Ghost[0m[2m charge?[0m[2m No,[0m[2m charge[0m[2m failed.[0m[2m Ghost[0m[2m delivery[0m[2m? Yes[0m[2m, inventory[0m[2m was decre[0m[2mmented but[0m[2m not[0m[2m charged[0m[2m. But[0m[2m this[0m[2m is[0m[2m the same[0m[2m as[0m[2m the first[0m[2m call[0m[2m crashing[0m[2m after[0m[2m decrement[0m[2m but before[0m[2m charge -[0m[2m the inventory[0m[2m is[0m[2m permanently[0m[2m decre[0m[2mmented for[0m[2m a[0m[2m failed order[0m[2m.[0m[2m
     
     Wait[0m[2m, that's[0m[2m a problem[0m[2m.[0m[2m If we[0m[2m crash after[0m[2m `de[0m[2mcrement_order[0m[2m` but[0m[2m before `[0m[2mcharge`,[0m[2m and then[0m[2m retry,[0m[2m the retry[0m[2m sees the[0m[2m order as[0m[2m already[0m[2m processed and[0m[2m skips[0m[2m decrement[0m[2m. Then[0m[2m charge[0m[2m might[0m[2m fail[0m[2m,[0m[2m and we[0m[2m return False[0m[2m. But[0m[2m the[0m[2m inventory stays[0m[2m decre[0m[2mmented.[0m[2m That's a[0m[2m leak[0m[2m,[0m[2m but not[0m[2m a ghost[0m[2m charge ([0m[2msince charge[0m[2m failed).[0m[2m
     
     If[0m[2m charge succeeds[0m[2m on retry[0m[2m, we[0m[2m have a[0m[2m charge and[0m[2m a delivery[0m[2m. Good[0m[2m.
     
     So[0m[2m the only[0m[2m bad[0m[2m case is[0m[2m: crash[0m[2m after decrement[0m[2m but[0m[2m before charge[0m[2m, and[0m[2m then[0m[2m no[0m[2m retry happens[0m[2m. Inventory[0m[2m is leaked[0m[2m.[0m[2m But this[0m[2m is a[0m[2m crash[0m[2m recovery[0m[2m issue,[0m[2m not a[0m[2m race condition[0m[2m issue.[0m[2m
     
     For the[0m[2m concurrent[0m[2m simulation and[0m[2m the stated[0m[2m requirements,[0m[2m this approach[0m[2m seems[0m[2m solid[0m[2m.
     
     But[0m[2m actually,[0m[2m for[0m[2m the simulation[0m[2m, the[0m[2m simpler approach[0m[2m (just[0m[2m reverse[0m[2m order[0m[2m in[0m[2m checkout[0m[2m, add[0m[2m locks to[0m[2m decrement[0m[2m and increment[0m[2m, and[0m[2m add duplicate[0m[2m protection[0m[2m to Payment[0m[2mGateway returning[0m[2m False[0m[2m) is[0m[2m also sufficient[0m[2m.[0m[2m The simulation[0m[2m doesn't test[0m[2m duplicate[0m[2m check[0m[2mouts.[0m[2m
     
     Let me[0m[2m decide[0m[2m which approach[0m[2m to use[0m[2m. The[0m[2m requirements[0m[2m say:[0m[2m
     - Inventory[0m[2m never goes[0m[2m below zero[0m[2m
     -[0m[2m Every successful[0m[2m charge corresponds[0m[2m to exactly[0m[2m one item[0m[2m delivered[0m[2m
     - No[0m[2m order is[0m[2m charged more[0m[2m than once[0m[2m
     
     The[0m[2m simpler[0m[2m approach satisfies[0m[2m all[0m[2m three[0m[2m for the[0m[2m simulation[0m[2m. But[0m[2m the "[0m[2mEvery[0m[2m successful charge[0m[2m corresponds to[0m[2m exactly one[0m[2m item delivered[0m[2m" requirement[0m[2m could[0m[2m be violated[0m[2m if the[0m[2m same `[0m[2morder_id[0m[2m` is[0m[2m used[0m[2m in[0m[2m multiple `[0m[2mcheckout`[0m[2m calls and[0m[2m `[0m[2mcharge`[0m[2m returns `[0m[2mTrue`[0m[2m for duplicates[0m[2m.
     
     Wait[0m[2m, with[0m[2m the simple[0m[2m approach and[0m[2m `charge[0m[2m` returning[0m[2m `False[0m[2m` for[0m[2m duplicates:[0m[2m
     - If[0m[2m checkout[0m[2m is called[0m[2m twice with[0m[2m same order[0m[2m_id,[0m[2m and[0m[2m first[0m[2m succeeds,[0m[2m second gets[0m[2m `[0m[2mFalse[0m[2m` from[0m[2m charge,[0m[2m increments inventory[0m[2m back,[0m[2m returns False[0m[2m.
     -[0m[2m First[0m[2m checkout[0m[2m: charge[0m[2m succeeded[0m[2m, delivery[0m[2m succeeded[0m[2m.[0m[2m 
     - Second[0m[2m checkout:[0m[2m charge failed[0m[2m (duplicate[0m[2m), delivery[0m[2m undone[0m[2m.[0m[2m
     
     This is[0m[2m actually correct[0m[2m! There's[0m[2m one[0m[2m charge[0m[2m and one[0m[2m delivery for[0m[2m that[0m[2m order_id[0m[2m. The[0m[2m second call[0m[2m just[0m[2m fails.[0m[2m
     
     But what[0m[2m if the[0m[2m first checkout[0m[2m crashed[0m[2m AFTER charge[0m[2m but BEFORE[0m[2m decrement[0m[2m? With[0m[2m the simple[0m[2m approach,[0m[2m we[0m[2m decrement first[0m[2m, so[0m[2m this[0m[2m can't happen[0m[2m.
     
     What[0m[2m if the[0m[2m first checkout[0m[2m crashed AFTER[0m[2m decrement[0m[2m but BEFORE[0m[2m charge?[0m[2m Then:[0m[2m
     - Stock[0m[2m is decre[0m[2mmented but[0m[2m not[0m[2m charged[0m[2m.[0m[2m
     - Retry[0m[2m:[0m[2m decrement succeeds[0m[2m (stock[0m[2m decre[0m[2mmented again[0m[2m!),[0m[2m charge succeeds[0m[2m.[0m[2m
     - Now[0m[2m we have[0m[2m 2[0m[2m decre[0m[2mments for[0m[2m 1[0m[2m charge.[0m[2m If[0m[2m stock[0m[2m was tight[0m[2m, this[0m[2m could[0m[2m cause issues[0m[2m.
     
     Actually[0m[2m, if[0m[2m the first[0m[2m call[0m[2m crashed after[0m[2m decrement[0m[2m,[0m[2m the stock[0m[2m is already[0m[2m lower[0m[2m. The[0m[2m retry would[0m[2m decrement again[0m[2m. That's[0m[2m wrong[0m[2m.[0m[2m
     
     This[0m[2m is why[0m[2m id[0m[2mempotency[0m[2m in[0m[2m `de[0m[2mcrement`[0m[2m is important[0m[2m. With[0m[2m `[0m[2mdecrement[0m[2m_order`,[0m[2m the retry[0m[2m would see[0m[2m the order[0m[2m as[0m[2m already processed[0m[2m and not[0m[2m decrement again[0m[2m.
     
     OK[0m[2m, I'll[0m[2m go[0m[2m with the[0m[2m `de[0m[2mcrement_order[0m[2m` approach[0m[2m. It's[0m[2m more robust[0m[2m and correct[0m[2m.
     
